# Stage 13 — Preproduction stage 1 spec

Read `references/epub_assets_figures_tables.md`, `references/chapter_title_policy.md`,
and (for cover/frontmatter) any private_use overlay references if present.

Write `preproduction/stage1/production_spec.md` covering:
- cover plan (producer line: `LifeBook 书坊 译制`, or the private-use producer line
  if `publication_mode=private_use`)
- book-info / frontmatter page plan
- fonts, headings hierarchy, body typography
- figures/tables handling and asset inventory
- OPF metadata (title, author, language={{ target_lang }}, identifier, rights)
- chapter navigation labels (short nav titles per the title policy)

Use `metadata/book.yaml` only as an ingest-time input. Write the final decisions to
`metadata/finalized_book.yaml` as a YAML mapping with these keys: `title`, `authors`,
`language`, `identifier`, `rights`, and `publisher`. The title, language, identifier,
and rights must be non-empty; the identifier must be stable rather than generated by
the EPUB builder. Keep the production specification consistent with this YAML.
You MUST call `write_file` for both `preproduction/stage1/production_spec.md` and
`metadata/finalized_book.yaml` in this attempt, even when those canonical paths already
exist. Their existence may represent an obsolete generation, not completion of this
Action. The tools stage replacement generations without mutating canonical files; the
controller validates and promotes the complete pair atomically.

Exit condition: `preproduction/stage1/production_spec.md` and
`metadata/finalized_book.yaml` exist and contain the same complete frontmatter and
metadata decisions.
Stop for controller validation.
